<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n93473" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σᾰφην-ής</span></b> , 
			Dor.
		
		<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σᾰφην-ᾱνής</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ές</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b>
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σαφής</span>
			, <i><span class="en">
				Id.
				<u>Pers.</u>
				635
			</span></i> (lyr.), <i><span class="en">
				738
			</span></i> (troch.), <i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>Tr.</u>
				892
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὸ ς</span>. the <i>plain
			truth</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Pi.
				<u>O.</u>
				10(11).55
			</span></i>: <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σαφήνη</span> is corrupt in <i><span class="en">
				A.
				<u>Ch.</u>
				197
			</span></i>, cf. foreg. Adv.
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-νῶς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Thgn.
					963
				</span></i>
			 (but <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-νέως</span> is the better
			reading); 
				Ion.
			
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-νέως</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hdt.
				</span></i>
			 (who never has the Adj.), with the Verbs <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εἰπεῖν, λέγεσθαι, ἐξαγγέλλεσθαι</span>,
				<i><span class="en">
				1.140
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				3.122
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				6.82
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὰ λοιπά σοι φράσω ς</span>.
				<i><span class="en">
				A.
				<u>Pr.</u>
				781
			</span></i>.</div>
